course: dictionary
lesson: 13293
title: Granulated
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Granulated tells you something has been broken into small grains, tiny bits you can see and feel. «The recipe needs two spoons of granulated sugar.» The word granulated tells you the sugar is in small grains, not in one lump or as a fine powder.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Sugar that is stirred into a cake mix is a grainy kind of sugar. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The recipe needs two spoons of small grains of sugar.» If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Granulated sugar is the ordinary white sugar you find in a kitchen cupboard. It is different from icing sugar, which is a fine powder. Always check the sentence, because the same word can be used in different subjects, such as science.
fact: Granulated means in the form of small grains.
fact: Granulated sugar is ordinary white sugar with small crystals.
fact: In science, granulated can mean made into small grains, or having a grainy surface.
fact: «Granulated» is the past form of the verb granulate, so «The cook granulated the sugar» means she made it into small grains.
fact: Icing sugar is a fine powder, so it is different from granulated sugar.
exercise: «The recipe asks for 100 grams of granulated sugar.» What does granulated mean here? | Like a liquid | *Made of tiny grains | Very cold | Soft and sticky
exercise: «The scientist granulated the salt until it looked like sand.» What does granulated mean? | *Broken into small grains | Melted into a liquid | Made very big | Painted bright blue
exercise: Maya says granulated sugar is the same as icing sugar. Is she right? | No, granulated sugar is a liquid | Yes, they are exactly the same | Yes, both are brown | *No, icing sugar is a fine powder, and granulated sugar has small grains
test: «Dad sprinkled granulated sugar on the pancakes.» What does granulated tell you about the sugar? | It is a wet syrup | It is one big lump | It is green | *It is made of small grains
test: Which word means made into small grains? | *granulated | frozen | sticky | smooth
exam: Which sentence uses granulated correctly? | *The sugar was granulated into tiny grains | The dog granulated loudly | The sky was granulated and blue | The cake was granulated in the oven
